{"results":[{"url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-fix/wp/2016/09/27/a-brief-history-of-donald-trumps-denialist-position-on-climate-change/","final_url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-fix/wp/2016/09/27/a-brief-history-of-donald-trumps-denialist-position-on-climate-change/","title":"A brief history of Donald Trump’s denialist position on climate change","description":"He's always been a skeptic — but for business reasons, not political ones.","language":"en","text":"Democracy Dies in Darkness\n\nBy  Philip Bump\n\nOne of the most readily debunkable comments Donald Trump made during the first presidential debate was his claim that he had never blamed global warming on China.\n\n\"Donald thinks that climate change is a hoax perpetrated by the Chinese,\" Hillary Clinton said at one point. \"I think it's real.\"\n\n---","author":"Philip Bump","published_date":"2016-09-27T17:20:55.000Z","latency_ms":1161.96384199975,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}